<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Book of Proverbs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Book of Proverbs is a book of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>, part of its wisdom literature, made up of collections of moral and practical sayings. Several collections are attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a>, others to the men of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hezekiah">Hezekiah</a> and to sages such as Agur and Lemuel; scholars usually date its final compilation to the Persian period, though parts may be older.</p></div>
